<title>AFGHANISTAN: Afghan Taleban burn movies.</title>
<headline>Afghan Taleban burn movies.</headline>
<dateline>KABUL 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Afghanistan's purist Islamic militia Taleban emptied one of Kabul's main cinema of movies on Monday and burned them outside.</p>
<p>The Taleban announced the imposition of Islam's stern Sharia law after they took the relatively liberal capital two weeks ago and banned television and music.</p>
<p>Taleban members carrying armfuls of what they said were Indian and Western movies to throw on the bonfire said the downtown Zaynab cinema would be turned into a mosque.</p>
<p>The movie burning almost had fatal consequences as bullets began to explode in the flames. One hit a soundman for a French television channel just above the eye.</p>
<p>Doctors said he would recover his vision, but there was no immediate explanation of how the bullets got into the bonfire.</p>
</text>
